etours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Vermilion City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Lt. Surge: the lightning American — ELECTRIC-types; ground moves shut his whole act down YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, beat Brock in Pewter (Boulder Badge), fought up Route 3 and through the Mt. Moon cave — a real maze you nearly got lost in — reached Cerulean City, and beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Now you\'re after your third gym.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Lorelei AND Lance down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "TM03 teaches WATER PULSE. Use it on an aquatic POK.MON!"; "KIRA put the TM03 in the TM CASE.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Vermilion City for the Thunder Badge. Next: You CRUSHED that last gym — ride the momentum, go straight for Lt. Surge in Vermilion City; the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Vermilion City, beat Lt. Surge for the Thunder Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L30), caterpie the butterfree (L10), rattata (L13), spearow (L14), abra (L13), ekans (L13). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.. HEADS UP — you just chose \'talk_npc\' and 