   [campaign]    [soul] ORACLE decision: kind=action ctx={'place': 'You\'re on Route 4 — outdoors under open sky (a town with a Pokémon Center; tall grass around — wild Pokémon live in it).. From here: SOUTH → Route 3 — wild Pokémon to catch/train; EAST → Cerulean City — a Mart, a Pokémon Center. Places you\'ve been with wild Pokémon you can walk back to: Route 24; an unfamiliar area; Route 2. You can walk to anywhere you\'ve already been.. HOW POKÉMON WORKS (what you\'re playing for): the GOAL is to earn 8 Gym Badges, beat the Elite Four, and roll the credits — that\'s beating the game. You build a TEAM of up to 6 Pokémon you like AND that cover each other (types/roles) — a solo carry with a dead-weight bench is a losing setup; a real trainer fields a balanced, levelled squad. CATCHING wild Pokémon is central (\'gotta catch \'em all\') — you catch to build that team and to fill the Pokédex. When you meet a wild Pokémon, weigh it: is it cool/strong/useful, does it cover a gap, is it better than a bench-warmer? — keep your best ~6, and build a squad you actually like. THE ARC: build a team -> beat the 8 gyms prepared -> Elite Four -> credits. ALSO NORMAL: you entered your own name (and your rival\'s) when the game began — people in this world knowing your names is ordinary, not a mystery to react to. RIGHT NOW your team is thin/lopsided (a strong lead but weak or too few others) — that\'s why tough trainers wall you. Building up a real squad (catch a good new teammate, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 3 of 8 — next is Lt. Surge in Vermilion City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Vermilion City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Lt. Surge: the lightning American — ELECTRIC-types; ground moves shut his whole act down YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, beat Brock in Pewter (Boulder Badge), fought up Route 3 and through the Mt. Moon cave — a real maze you nearly got lost in — reached Cerulean City, and beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Now you\'re after your third gym.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Lorelei AND Lance down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "TM03 teaches WATER PULSE. Use it on an aquatic POK.MON!"; "KIRA put the TM03 in the TM CASE.". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Vermilion City for the Thunder Badge. Next: You CRUSHED that last gym — ride the momentum, go straight for Lt. Surge in Vermilion City; the trainers on the way are your training. Bigger picture: Reach Vermilion City, beat Lt. Surge for the Thunder Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L30), caterpie the butterfree (L10), rattata (L13), spearow (L14), abra (L13), ekans (L13). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.', 'progress': "2 badge(s) earned (Boulder, Cascade). Next gym: Lt. Surge of Vermilion City. Pokédex: 9 caught. She's two badges down, a quarter of the way (of 8 badges, then the Elite Four).", 'party': 'wartortle (L30), caterpie the butterfree (L10), rattata (L13), spearow (L14), abra (L13), ekans (L13)', 'goal': {'short': "You're ready — stop grinding and head to Vermilion City for the Thunder Badge", 'medium': 'You CRUSHED that last gym — ride the momentum, go straight for Lt. Surge in Vermilion City; the trainers on the way are your training', 'long': 'Reach Vermilion City, beat Lt. Surge for the Thunder Badge'}} options=['talk_npc']

